WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:09.900
One human cell holds billions of protein molecules, from about 10,000 kinds.

2
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:16.980
You want one. Which molecule is doing this job, and can you hold it in a tube, free

3
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:17.980
of everything else?

4
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.500
In the 1920s, leading chemists held that enzymes were not proteins.

5
00:00:24.483 --> 00:00:30.583
Start with an assay, a way to detect the target in a tube where you cannot see it.

6
00:00:31.303 --> 00:00:37.403
Lactate dehydrogenase consumes NADH, which absorbs light at 340 nanometres.

7
00:00:38.243 --> 00:00:41.283
NAD+ does not, so absorbance falls.

8
00:00:42.443 --> 00:00:44.243
Then break the cells and spin.

9
00:00:44.983 --> 00:00:51.943
A gentle spin pellets nuclei, a harder one mitochondria, a harder one the smallest vesicles.

11
00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:55.663
After each step, run the assay again.

12
00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:02.183
Specific activity is units of activity divided by milligrams of total protein.

13
00:01:03.103 --> 00:01:07.643
It rises when a step removes contaminant without destroying the target.

14
00:01:09.223 --> 00:01:15.383
Salting out uses solubility: ammonium sulfate drops proteins out at different salt

15
00:01:15.383 --> 00:01:18.283
concentrations, leaving many contaminants behind.

16
00:01:19.203 --> 00:01:21.483
Gel filtration uses size.

17
00:01:22.503 --> 00:01:27.123
Large proteins cannot enter the pores, so take the short path and elute first.

18
00:01:28.263 --> 00:01:29.263
Small ones come last.

19
00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:34.827
Ion exchange uses charge, and opposite charges stick.

20
00:01:36.247 --> 00:01:41.287
Below its pI, a protein is net positive and binds a cation exchanger.

21
00:01:42.247 --> 00:01:46.987
Above it, the protein is net negative and binds an anion exchanger.

22
00:01:47.887 --> 00:01:49.847
Raise the salt, and it lets go.

23
00:01:51.147 --> 00:01:55.367
Affinity uses beads that carry something only the target recognizes.

24
00:01:56.057 --> 00:02:00.947
The target binds, the rest flows through, and free ligand displaces it.

25
00:02:01.607 --> 00:02:04.167
If you know a binding partner, start with affinity.

26
00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.520
Read the purification table.

27
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:14.080
Total protein and activity both fall, because protein is lost, and some enzyme with

28
00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:18.220
it. Specific activity should rise at every step.

29
00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:25.800
In this idealised example, it climbs from about 10 to 30,000 units per milligram, a

30
00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:30.560
3,000-fold purification, while yield slides to roughly a third.

31
00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:38.320
In Benovic's real run, four columns gave about 20,000-fold, with 12% recovered.

32
00:02:39.233 --> 00:02:41.893
Purity can strip away a partner.

33
00:02:42.813 --> 00:02:48.933
Benovic's kinase batch, purified only 350-fold, cut a receptor's G-protein

34
00:02:48.933 --> 00:02:56.213
activation by up to 80%. The 20,000-fold pure enzyme cut it far less, because a

35
00:02:56.213 --> 00:02:59.573
second protein, arrestin, had apparently been removed.

36
00:03:00.253 --> 00:03:02.713
So test the pure fraction on the effect.

37
00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:09.123
In 1926, Sumner crystallized urease from jack bean extract.

38
00:03:09.943 --> 00:03:15.063
Dissolved, the crystals gave tests for protein and very high urease activity.

39
00:03:16.103 --> 00:03:17.503
Enzymes can be proteins.

40
00:03:18.663 --> 00:03:25.363
In January 1922, James Collip raised alcohol in steps to trap insulin in a semipure

41
00:03:25.363 --> 00:03:29.343
form, and his extract worked in patient Leonard Thompson.

42
00:03:29.343 --> 00:03:32.763
Purification made insulin a drug.

43
00:03:33.617 --> 00:03:37.677
Stanley Cohen's group ran an EGF affinity column.

44
00:03:38.377 --> 00:03:43.717
Receptor, kinase and substrate came out together, and the kinase phosphorylated

45
00:03:43.717 --> 00:03:48.377
tyrosine. Labelling later showed the receptor is the kinase.

46
00:03:49.417 --> 00:03:56.397
In 1997, Alessi, Cohen and colleagues purified a kinase 500,000-fold.

47
00:03:57.097 --> 00:04:02.117
It activates Akt only with certain lipids, which a purified system can test

48
00:04:02.117 --> 00:04:06.917
directly. A pure fraction speaks only for the assay you followed.

49
00:04:07.677 --> 00:04:09.217
Test it on the biological effect.
